# The exported player's first start: the shaders the game needs are prepared ONCE, as a step of its own, instead of in front of the game's progress screen at the first boot (268 s on an iPhone 15 Pro for Mario Kart 8
# Deluxe, shown as "Preparing the game" and, with a short list, as a freeze of 85 s at 0 fps in the first race: device tests 2026-11-19). A player has its own bundle id and so an empty Metal cache, which cannot be
# shipped (a cache copied from the player into iBuilder gave no hit). So the player compiles, at its first launch, exactly the libraries the host prepares at a boot (the pack's seed list, this phone's learned list
# pso_user.tsv, what was used) with the same options as the host (GameAppWarm.cs), four workers at UserInitiated QoS, waiting only at thermal Serious; a progress bar and the status line on its title screen; the
# continued-processing task keeps it going when the player leaves the app; it does not wait for the game files (the .romfs can be copied meanwhile); prepared.tsv (app build + chain) says it is done; a Play pressed
# meanwhile asks "Wait" or "Play anyway". Only an exported player does it (the main app has the manual "Prepare the shaders…"). Applies after 0060.
